        "jptr:compound-cbx",
        "jptr:compound-thch",
        "jptr:compound-cbl",
        "jptr:compound-cbga"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "jptr:compound-rare",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": "jptr:compound-taxonomy",
      "skos:topConceptOf": "jptr:compound-taxonomy",
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Rare Cannabinoids",
          "@language": "en"
        },
        {
          "@value": "レアカンナビノイド",
          "@language": "ja"
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "compound_rare",
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Reserved for rare cannabinoids, i.e. the many phytocannabinoids found only in trace amounts (CBDP, THCP and similar). INTENTIONALLY EMPTY: no rare cannabinoid is registered as a concept yet, so this category records a dimension the taxonomy intends to cover rather than a gap or an oversight. Every other category lists its members in skos:narrower.",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "jptr:compound-semisynthetic",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": "jptr:compound-taxonomy",
      "skos:topConceptOf": "jptr:compound-taxonomy",
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Semi-Synthetic Cannabinoids",
          "@language": "en"
        },
        {
          "@value": "半合成カンナビノイド",
          "@language": "ja"
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "compound_semisynthetic",
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Cannabinoids obtained by chemically modifying a natural cannabinoid: HHC, THC-O, H4CBH, HHBD and THCNM. Classified by production route, which is why HHC sits here although it is also a hydrogenated cannabinoid. Chemical class is a separate dimension (jptr:chemical-class-taxonomy): HHC, H4CBH and HHBD are chemclass_hydrogenated, THC-O is chemclass_acetate, and THCNM has no formalized chemical class. THCNM's placement is provisional: both market-reported identities describe a substituted derivative of a phytocannabinoid, but the identity itself is unconfirmed (see its scopeNote).",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:narrower": [
        "jptr:compound-hhc",
        "jptr:compound-thc-o",
        "jptr:compound-h4cbh",
        "jptr:compound-hhbd",
        "jptr:compound-thcnm"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "jptr:compound-synthetic",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": "jptr:compound-taxonomy",
      "skos:topConceptOf": "jptr:compound-taxonomy",
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Synthetic Cannabinoids",
          "@language": "en"
        },
        {
          "@value": "合成カンナビノイド",
          "@language": "ja"
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "compound_synthetic",
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Cannabinoids with no natural counterpart: HHCH, CRDP and CRDH.",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:narrower": [
        "jptr:compound-hhch",
        "jptr:compound-crdp",
        "jptr:compound-crdh"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "jptr:compound-endocannabinoid",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": "jptr:compound-taxonomy",
      "skos:topConceptOf": "jptr:compound-taxonomy",
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Endocannabinoids",
          "@language": "en"
        },
        {
          "@value": "エンドカンナビノイド",
          "@language": "ja"
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "compound_endocannabinoid",
      "skos:scopeNote": {
        "@value": "Endogenous signalling molecules of the endocannabinoid system: anandamide and 2-AG. Listed because they are described in the same literature, not because they are administered products.",
        "@language": "en"
      },
      "skos:narrower": [
        "jptr:compound-anandamide",
        "jptr:compound-2ag"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "jptr:compound-identity-unverified",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": "jptr:compound-taxonomy",
      "skos:topConceptOf": "jptr:compound-taxonomy",
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Identity-Unverified Registered Terms (registration state)",
          "@language": "en"
        },
        {
          "@value": "同一性未確認の登録語（登録状態）",
          "@language": "ja"
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "compound_identity_unverified",
      "skos:scopeNote": [
        {
          "@value": "An ADMINISTRATIVE registration-state category, not a route/origin or chemical classification. Its members are search terms the owner named for this study whose single-substance chemical identity is UNCONFIRMED in this repository. Placing a term here records only that the string is registered and queryable: it makes no claim about route or origin, natural occurrence, chemical class, structure, synonym relationships or regulatory status, and it neither asserts that the term names a distinct substance nor that a substance behind the string exists. Membership is not a judgement that a term is rare, minor, semi-synthetic or synthetic, and it never substitutes for one of those categories; when evidence arrives, move the term to the category that evidence supports. No identifier property and no `skos:exactMatch` are assigned to a member's taxonomy concept, and no chemical-class link is asserted; CAS / PubChem / UNII / ChEBI / Wikidata / IUPAC values quoted in a member's scopeNote are recorded evidence in `docs/provenance/compound-taxonomy.md`, not identifier properties, and per-isomer registry records for a family-scoped member belong in the provenance ledger, never on the concept. Membership itself establishes no synonym relationship. A member's skos:altLabel is a concept-level record: an alternate or search-topic label that the owner confirmed needs its own recorded basis in that concept's scopeNote (for example an owner-confirmed intended meaning), and it is neither implied by, nor does it add a synonym claim to, this administrative placement. For a family-scoped member such a label does not assert that the family denotes one chemical structure. A term is registered here because the owner named it, not because its identity was established. Decision record: ISS-20261111-TAX-040, which supersedes the ISS-20261015-TAX-027 non-registration decision for THCP. A member may also be a term the owner confirmed only as an isomer-unspecified homologue family, or as an isomer-unspecified ester (acetate) of one: the term then denotes no single substance and no single external record, so it stays here and its own scopeNote records the family scope; that statement is the term's documented search scope, not a route/origin placement, not a chemical-class link, and not a claim about any individual result. A family-scoped member's scopeNote may also record that its per-isomer substances fall within a documented statutory structural group; that is a statement about those isomers, not a regulatory classification performed by this placement. A member may also be a specific positional-isomer designation (for example a Δ8 or Δ9 term) that the owner confirmed as a search topic, where this change did not verify a single external registry record for the registered string: the term then records the search topic and the published nomenclature, while the category still makes no chemical claim and assigns no identifier property. This batch also registered a specifically named stereochemical configuration whose only recorded basis is a nomenclature or WHO review of possible configurations, with no per-configuration registry record and no product identification, and an isomer-unspecified acetate of a homologue family whose individual positional structures the repository does not enumerate: in both cases the concept records the search topic and the published nomenclature, and this category still makes no chemical, route, regulatory or product claim.",
          "@language": "en"
        },
        {
          "@value": "経路・由来や化学分類ではなく、**管理上の登録状態**カテゴリ。members は owner が本研究のために名指しした検索語のうち、リポジトリ内で**単一物質としての**化学的同一性が**未確認**のものである。ここに置くことは「その文字列を登録し照会可能にした」ことだけを記録する。経路・由来、天然存在、化学クラス、構造、別名関係、規制状態について何も主張せず、語が別個の物質を指すことや、文字列の背後に物質が存在することの主張でもない。希少・マイナー・半合成・合成のいずれかであるという判断でもなく、これらのカテゴリの代替にもならない。根拠が得られたら、その根拠が支えるカテゴリへ移す。member の taxonomy 概念には識別子プロパティも `skos:exactMatch` も割り当てず、化学クラスへのリンクも主張しない。member の scopeNote に引用した CAS 番号・PubChem CID・UNII・ChEBI ID・Wikidata QID・IUPAC 名は `docs/provenance/compound-taxonomy.md` に記録された証拠であり、識別子プロパティではない。ファミリーとして登録した語の異性体ごとのレジストリ記録は台帳に置き、概念には付けない。membership 自体は同義関係を確立しない。member の `skos:altLabel` は概念レベルの記録であり、owner が確認した別名・検索トピックの表記には、その概念の scopeNote に独自の根拠（例: owner が確認した意図された意味）を要する。カテゴリ所属から導かれるものでも、所属に同義の主張を加えるものでもない。ファミリーとして登録した語では、そうした別名はファミリーが単一の化学構造を指す主張ではない。ここへの登録は owner が語を名指ししたことが理由であり、同一性が確定したことが理由ではない。決定記録: ISS-20261111-TAX-040（THCP については ISS-20261015-TAX-027 の非登録判断を置換）。また、owner が**異性体未指定の同族体ファミリー**、またはその異性体未指定のエステル（アセテート）体としてのみ確認した語もここに置く。その語は単一物質も単一の外部レコードも指さないため本カテゴリに留まり、ファミリーの範囲は当該概念の scopeNote に記録する。その記載は検索語の文書化された範囲であり、経路／由来の配置でも、化学クラスへのリンクでも、個々の検索結果についての主張でもない。ファミリーとして登録した語の scopeNote は、異性体ごとの物質が文書化された法令上の構造グループに該当することを記録する場合があるが、それは当該異性体についての記載であり、本配置が行う規制分類ではない。また、owner が**位置異性体を明示した検索トピック**（例: Δ8 体・Δ9 体の語）として確認し、本変更では登録文字列について単一の外部レジストリ記録を検証していない語もここに置く。その場合、当該概念は検索トピックと公表された命名を記録するが、本カテゴリは化学的主張を行わず、識別子プロパティも割り当てない。また本バッチは、記録された根拠が命名標準または WHO の可能な配置のレビューのみで、配置ごとの registry record も製品同定も無い**特定の立体配置**、および個々の位置異性体の構造をリポジトリが列挙していない**同族体ファミリーの異性体未指定アセテート**も登録した。いずれの場合も概念は検索トピックと公表された命名を記録するものであり、本カテゴリは化学・経路・規制・製品について何も主張しない。",
          "@language": "ja"
        }
      ],
      "skos:narrower": [
        "jptr:compound-thcb",
        "jptr:compound-thcp",
