      ],
      "skos:notation": "compound_cbga",
      "skos:scopeNote": [
        {
          "@value": "`CBGa` is the owner's term for **cannabigerolic acid** (standard spelling CBGA), confirmed by the owner on 2026-11-11. Identity and identifiers were verified against ChEBI 67081 (cannabigerolic acid), Wikidata Q27135612 (en label 'cannabigerolic acid', CAS 25555-57-1, PubChem CID 6449999, ChEBI 67081, formula C22H32O4), the FDA GSRS record for UNII 80I4ZM847Y (substanceClass chemical, definitionLevel COMPLETE; names CANNABIGEROLIC ACID / CBGA; CAS 25555-57-1, PubChem CID 6449999, formula C22H32O4) and PubChem CID 6449999 ('Cannabigerolic Acid', C22H32O4). The owner's spelling `CBGa` (lowercase 'a') is preserved exactly in the labels and in the registered query strings; it names the same substance as CBGA, is not a second substance, and no case normalization is applied to raw or query records. CBGA is an acidic phytocannabinoid and the biosynthetic precursor from which other cannabinoid acids are formed (ChEBI: 'a biosynthetic precursor to delta-9-tetrahydrocannabinol'; PMID 31686510 describes the phytocannabinoid acids, including CBGA, as the dominant forms in the plant; PMID 35887277). CBG is the decarboxylated neutral product of CBGA, not a synonym: heating converts CBGA to CBG (PMID 35887277; PMID 36397993), so the two are recorded as distinct concepts. Placement in compound-minor records only 'a phytocannabinoid other than the major pair'; no chemical-class link is asserted and no regulatory status is claimed. **No skos:related link to compound_cbg is asserted:** the precursor/product relation is recorded in this note only, and the compound_cbg external-identifier mapping is unresolved (separate follow-up). **Query limitation:** Google Trends and YouTube series for `CBGa` measure occurrences of that literal string, not verified cannabigerolic acid content; the two Google Trends attempts returned no series (NO_DATA), and the existing samples are string-match observations. Basis and source record: docs/provenance/compound-taxonomy.md (ISS-20261111-TAX-040 addendum).",
          "@language": "en"
        },
        {
          "@value": "`CBGa` は owner が **cannabigerolic acid（カンナビゲロール酸、標準表記 CBGA）** を指す語として 2026-11-11 に確認した登録語である。同一性と識別子は ChEBI 67081（cannabigerolic acid）、Wikidata Q27135612（en: cannabigerolic acid、CAS 25555-57-1、PubChem CID 6449999、ChEBI 67081、分子式 C22H32O4）、FDA GSRS の UNII 80I4ZM847Y 記録（substanceClass chemical、definitionLevel COMPLETE、名称 CANNABIGEROLIC ACID / CBGA、CAS 25555-57-1、PubChem CID 6449999、分子式 C22H32O4）、PubChem CID 6449999（Cannabigerolic Acid、C22H32O4）で検証した。owner の表記 `CBGa`（小文字の `a`）はラベルと登録クエリ文字列でそのまま保存し、同じ物質を指す表記であって別物質ではなく、raw / query 記録に大文字小文字の正規化も適用しない。CBGA は他のカンナビノイド酸が生成される前段の酸性フィトカンナビノイドで（ChEBI: Δ9-THC の生合成前駆体、PMID 31686510 は CBGA を含むフィトカンナビノイド酸を植物中の主要な存在形と記述、PMID 35887277）、CBG は CBGA が脱炭酸した中性体であって別名ではない（加熱で CBGA から CBG が生じる。PMID 35887277 / PMID 36397993）。したがって両者を別概念として記録する。`compound_minor` への配置は「主要な 2 化合物以外のフィトカンナビノイド」という範囲だけを記録し、化学クラスへのリンクも規制状態も主張しない。**`compound_cbg` への `skos:related` は張らない:** 前駆体／生成物の関係は本 scopeNote の文章に留め、`compound_cbg` の外部識別子の対応は未解決である（別途の確認待ち）。**クエリの限界:** Google Trends / YouTube の `CBGa` 系列が測るのは文字列への一致であり、cannabigerolic acid の内容の確認ではない。Google Trends の 2 試行は NO_DATA を返し、既存サンプルは文字列一致の観測である。根拠と出所は docs/provenance/compound-taxonomy.md（ISS-20261111-TAX-040 追記）。",
          "@language": "ja"
        }
      ],
      "skos:exactMatch": [
        "chebi:67081",
        "wikidata:Q27135612",
        "https://identifiers.org/unii:80I4ZM847Y"
      ]
    },
