        {
          "@value": "`Δ8-THCJD` is the owner's search term, registered on 2026-11-15 (ISS-20261115-TAX-045) as one of the 27 forms the owner enumerated for registration from the study's candidate-form inventory in `datasets/cannabinoid-raw-collection`. The term is a registered search string, not a substance identification: the single-substance chemical identity remains UNCONFIRMED. The evidence recorded for this form in the study inventory is a registry record together with a product analysis: PubChem CID 102024084, CAS 431041-39-3 and Wikidata Q114242092, and Tanaka & Kikura-Hanajiri 2024, which identified the Δ8 form by NMR in products distributed in Japan (ISS-20261111-TAX-042). That is an analysis of specific products, not this study's observation and not a claim about any query result; the study term is the C8 homologue designation, and this row is the Δ8 positional form only. No identifier property and no `skos:exactMatch` are assigned to this taxonomy concept: any CAS / PubChem / UNII / ChEBI / Wikidata / IUPAC values quoted in this note are recorded evidence in `docs/provenance/compound-taxonomy.md`, were not re-verified in this change, and were not selected for the registered query. It stays in compound_identity_unverified, an administrative registration-state category, so this placement asserts no route/origin, natural occurrence, chemical class, structure, synonym, pharmacology, safety or regulatory status, and it asserts no relation to the inventory parent term `THCJD`: that grouping in the candidate table organised the rows and is not a structural or synonym claim. **Query limitation:** Google Trends and YouTube series for `Δ8-THCJD` / `Δ8-THCJD リキッド` measure occurrences of those literal strings; a matching result is not evidence of the Δ8 positional form content. Evidence that would move the term out of this category: a verified external record selected for the registered string, or a recorded source naming this form and its route/origin; the basis belongs in docs/provenance/compound-taxonomy.md.",
