      "skos:scopeNote": [
        {
          "@value": "`Δ8-THCP-O-acetate` is the owner's search term, registered on 2026-11-15 (ISS-20261115-TAX-045) as one of the 27 forms the owner enumerated for registration from the study's candidate-form inventory in `datasets/cannabinoid-raw-collection`. The term is a registered search string, not a substance identification: the single-substance chemical identity remains UNCONFIRMED. The evidence recorded for this form in the study inventory is a statutory structural group and a registry record: the attached list (別紙) of the 2024 MHLW ordinance (令和6年厚生労働省令第81号) lists the Δ8 acetate structure among newly designated substances, subject to the ordinance's narcotics exclusion, and PubChem CID 172874392 was recorded (ISS-20261111-TAX-042). CAS, GSRS and Wikidata were not confirmed, and product analytical identification of this isomer was not confirmed. A statutory structural listing is a legal structural fact, not a product detection, not this study's observation and not a classification of any result or query string. No identifier property and no `skos:exactMatch` are assigned to this taxonomy concept: any CAS / PubChem / UNII / ChEBI / Wikidata / IUPAC values quoted in this note are recorded evidence in `docs/provenance/compound-taxonomy.md`, were not re-verified in this change, and were not selected for the registered query. It stays in compound_identity_unverified, an administrative registration-state category, so this placement asserts no route/origin, natural occurrence, chemical class, structure, synonym, pharmacology, safety or regulatory status, and it asserts no relation to the inventory parent term `THCPO`: that grouping in the candidate table organised the rows and is not a structural or synonym claim. **Query limitation:** Google Trends and YouTube series for `Δ8-THCP-O-acetate` / `Δ8-THCP-O-acetate リキッド` measure occurrences of those literal strings; a matching result is not evidence of this Δ8 acetate isomer content. Evidence that would move the term out of this category: a verified external record selected for the registered string, or a recorded product identification or route/origin source for this isomer; the basis belongs in docs/provenance/compound-taxonomy.md.",
