        {
          "@value": "`Δ8-THC` is the owner's search term, registered on 2026-11-15 (ISS-20261115-TAX-045) as one of the 27 forms the owner enumerated for registration from the study's candidate-form inventory in `datasets/cannabinoid-raw-collection`. The term is a registered search string, not a substance identification: the single-substance chemical identity remains UNCONFIRMED. The evidence recorded for this form in the study inventory is the published nomenclature standard together with the regulatory knowledge graph: the Δ8 series is one of the seven positions the standard distinguishes, the 2024 MHLW ordinance defines the Δ8 series (6a,7,10,10a-tetrahydro) as a structural group separate from the Δ9 series (6a,7,8,10a-tetrahydro) subject to the ordinance's narcotics exclusion, and the knowledge graph records CAS 5957-75-7 with natural occurrence confirmed (ISS-20261111-TAX-042). No form-level external registry record was selected for the taxonomy. The knowledge-graph entry and the statutory group definition are not this study's product analysis, not a product detection and not a statement about any result. No identifier property and no `skos:exactMatch` are assigned to this taxonomy concept: any CAS / PubChem / UNII / ChEBI / Wikidata / IUPAC values quoted in this note are recorded evidence in `docs/provenance/compound-taxonomy.md`, were not re-verified in this change, and were not selected for the registered query. It stays in compound_identity_unverified, an administrative registration-state category, so this placement asserts no route/origin, natural occurrence, chemical class, structure, synonym, pharmacology, safety or regulatory status, and it asserts no relation to the inventory parent term `THC`: that grouping in the candidate table organised the rows and is not a structural or synonym claim. **Query limitation:** Google Trends and YouTube series for `Δ8-THC` / `Δ8-THC リキッド` measure occurrences of those literal strings; a matching result is not evidence 