          "@value": "`Δ7-THC` is the owner's search term, registered on 2026-11-15 (ISS-20261115-TAX-045) as one of the 27 forms the owner enumerated for registration from the study's candidate-form inventory in `datasets/cannabinoid-raw-collection`. The term is a registered search string, not a substance identification: the single-substance chemical identity remains UNCONFIRMED. The evidence recorded for this form in the study inventory is the published nomenclature standard together with the regulatory knowledge graph: it is one of the seven positions the standard distinguishes, an old name Δ5-THC has a correspondence example whose structure still needs confirmation, the knowledge graph records natural occurrence unconfirmed, and no form-level external identifier was selected (no CAS number is recorded) (ISS-20261111-TAX-042). Product analysis was not confirmed, and the name correspondence is not an identity result. No identifier property and no `skos:exactMatch` are assigned to this taxonomy concept: any CAS / PubChem / UNII / ChEBI / Wikidata / IUPAC values quoted in this note are recorded evidence in `docs/provenance/compound-taxonomy.md`, were not re-verified in this change, and were not selected for the registered query. It stays in compound_identity_unverified, an administrative registration-state category, so this placement asserts no route/origin, natural occurrence, chemical class, structure, synonym, pharmacology, safety or regulatory status, and it asserts no relation to the inventory parent term `THC`: that grouping in the candidate table organised the rows and is not a structural or synonym claim. **Query limitation:** Google Trends and YouTube series for `Δ7-THC` / `Δ7-THC リキッド` measure occurrences of those literal strings; a matching result is not evidence of this positional isomer content. Evidence that would move the term out of this category: a verified form-level external record selected for the registered string, or a recorded source naming thi