        {
          "@value": "`(6aS,9S,10aS)-HHC` is the owner's search term, registered on 2026-11-15 (ISS-20261115-TAX-045) as one of the 27 forms the owner enumerated for registration from the study's candidate-form inventory in `datasets/cannabinoid-raw-collection`. The term is a registered search string, not a substance identification: the single-substance chemical identity remains UNCONFIRMED. The evidence recorded for this configuration in the study inventory is the WHO critical review: the WHO 47th ECDD (2024) §2C sets out the eight stereoisomers of HHC as possible configurations, and this one is one of the six beyond the two C-9 epimers recorded as the main components of CBD-derived product (configuration 6a=S / 9=S / 10a=S; the enantiomer of (6aR,9R,10aR)-HHC) (ISS-20261111-TAX-042). The review presents a set of possible configurations; it is not per-configuration registry evidence, not a product detection, not this study's analysis and not a claim about any result. No individual registry record was selected for this configuration and product identification of it was not confirmed. No identifier property and no `skos:exactMatch` are assigned to this taxonomy concept: any CAS / PubChem / UNII / ChEBI / Wikidata / IUPAC values quoted in this note are recorded evidence in `docs/provenance/compound-taxonomy.md`, were not re-verified in this change, and were not selected for the registered query. It stays in compound_identity_unverified, an administrative registration-state category, so this placement asserts no route/origin, natural occurrence, chemical class, structure, synonym, pharmacology, safety or regulatory status, and it asserts no relation to the inventory parent term `HHC`: that grouping in the candidate table organised the rows and is not a structural or synonym claim. **Query limitation:** Google Trends and YouTube series for `(6aS,9S,10aS)-HHC` / `(6aS,9S,10aS)-HHC リキッド` measure occurrences of those literal strings; a matching result is not evidence of this stereochemical configuration content. Evidence that would move the term out of this category: a per-configuration verified external record selected for the registered string, or a recorded product identification for this configuration; the basis belongs in docs/provenance/compound-taxonomy.md.",
